  "sourceQualifications": [
    "Current INS codes117153/117152/115153 independently identify these three imadas and the exact proposed Arabic aliases.",
    "ISIE2022 PDF page3 row1144 and rows1148-1152 use Marsa Hadayek/Medina official article forms; page4 rows1198/1199 use Carthage Byrsa بيرصا.",
    "The historical Interior directory corroborates both Marsa official article forms.",
    "Finance Ministry office address uses قرطاج بيرصة, supporting retention of the current primary spelling alongside the independently supported بيرصا alias.",
    "Administrative school/address usage supports name identity only. No official perimeter, point or timetable coordinate certification is claimed."
  ],
  "mechanism": "Existing name_tags replaces the consumed name-tag set. This proof preserves that complete set and adds only alt_name:ar. Existing child contextAliases inherit the extra name; no parentName changes. The existing small saved-name index gains three rows with unchanged current primary names and kind.",
  "preservation": "No generator change, automatic fuzzy/distance association, coordinates/default/group changes, retirement, boundary import or name normalization."
